On 2009-07-10, APLer <APLer@floor.tilde> wrote:
> Besides, recover is needed to be used *before* you play a backup in any
> case.

This is completely and demonstrably wrong.

If you back up the save file, you do not need to execute "recover" on it
before you play the save file.  You simply need to put the save file in
place of the old one.

The only need for "recover" is when your game crashes and leaves a large
number of uncompressed level files in the playground; the "recover"
utility reconstructs all those level files into a single save file,
which you can then restore and play as normal.

With regard to "recover"'s reliability; there are cases in which
"recover" cannot perform its task.  If one level file accidentally gets 
corrupted or deleted _during play_, Nethack will, the next time the
player attempts to enter that level (and thus attempts to load that
file), notify the player, delete all level files, and put an entry
in the score table listing that the player has died of "a trickery".
Recover is useless in this case; only a backup will restore your game.

